TITLE:: Ppetri
SUMMARY:: Experimental interleaved Petri-net firing
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events>Patterns>Patternarium
RELATED:: Classes/Pconstraint, Classes/PgraphWalk, Guides/Patternarium-Systems

DESCRIPTION::
Experimental: this API may change before 1.0.

At each item, chooses one enabled transition and atomically consumes/produces its tokens. Other enabled transitions remain for later interleaving; this does not model simultaneous or timed firing. Marking and transition names use Symbols. Places mentioned by arcs but absent from the initial marking begin with zero tokens.

Transition definitions are literal Events/Dictionaries with optional consume and produce place/token dictionaries, nonnegative finite weight (default 1), finite priority (default 0), value (default transition name), and nonnegative finite delta (default 1). Consume/produce counts must be nonnegative Integers. Inhibitor arcs and dynamic arc/priority Functions are unsupported.

Uniform ignores weights. Weighted samples positive weights. Priority first retains enabled transitions with the highest priority, then samples positive weights in that group; zero weights in that group can therefore cause a selectable deadlock. Transition names are sorted before selection for reproducible iteration order. Deadlock stop ends silently, warn warns then ends, and error throws.

Each fresh output Event contains transition, value, marking and delta. Marking is copied and never exposes internal mutable state. Transition values retain caller-owned identity. Per-place token counts and output indices have explicit machine-Integer bounds. Memory is O(places plus transition arcs); enabling checks scan the consume arcs, and each firing copies the marking. All mutable net state belongs to the stream.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: marking
Literal Dictionary/Event of place Symbols and nonnegative Integer tokens.
ARGUMENT:: transitions
Literal Dictionary/Event keyed by transition-name Symbols, with the transition definitions described above.
ARGUMENT:: length
Nonnegative Integer or inf, default inf; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: policy
weighted (default), uniform or priority; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: deadlock
stop (default), warn or error; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: output
Only event is currently supported. Evaluated once. Other once-sampled arguments accept literal values, Functions or Patterns.

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: storeArgs
Returns constructor arguments in public constructor order.
METHOD:: embedInStream
Yields values and returns the latest inval when the stream ends.

EXAMPLES::
code::
Ppetri((ready: 1), (start: (consume: (ready: 1), produce: (playing: 1)))).asStream.all;
::

Each firing sounds a note; pitch identifies the transition and duration follows its delta. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Ppetri / Value stream
var values = {
Ppetri((ready: 1), (start: (consume: (ready: 1), produce: (playing: 1)))).asStream.all;
}.value;
var labels;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
labels = values.collect { |e| e[\transition] }.as(Set).asArray.sort;
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \saw, degree: if(x[\value].isNumber) { x[\value] } { [0,2,4,7].wrapAt(labels.indexOf(x[\transition])) }, cutoff: 500+(x[\marking].values.sum*400), dur: x[\delta].min(0.3).max(0.05), amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Musical example
Load the main Guide example instruments first.
code::
(
Pbind(\instrument, \mallet,
    \fire, Pseed(Pseq([42]), Ppetri((fuel: 16), (
        low: (consume: (fuel: 1), value: 0, delta: 0.125),
        high: (consume: (fuel: 1), weight: 2, value: 7, delta: 0.125)), 16)),
    \degree, Pfunc { |e| e[\fire][\value] },
    \dur, Pfunc { |e| e[\fire][\delta] }).play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Concurrent independent processes
code::
Ppetri((a: 1, b: 1), (
    moveA: (consume: (a: 1), produce: (doneA: 1)),
    moveB: (consume: (b: 1), produce: (doneB: 1))
)).do { |event| event[\marking].postln };
::

SUBSECTION:: Synchronizing prerequisites
code::
Ppetri((ready: 1, cue: 1), (join: (consume: (ready: 1, cue: 1), produce: (playing: 1)))).asStream.all;
::

Each firing sounds a note; pitch identifies the transition and duration follows its delta. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
